{'symbol': 'WFC', 'date': '2021-06-17 17:05:00', 'title': 'JULIE CAPERTON NAMED HEAD OF WELLS FARGO PRIVATE BANK FOR WELLS FARGO WEALTH & INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT (WIM)', 'text': "SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--WELLS FARGO & COMPANY (NYSE: WFC) TODAY ANNOUNCED JULIE CAPERTON AS HEAD OF WELLS FARGO PRIVATE BANK, A DIVISION OF WEALTH & INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT (WIM). THIS IS IN ADDITION TO CAPERTON'S CURRENT ROLE AS HEAD OF THE BANKING, LENDING & TRUST CENTER OF EXCELLENCE FOR WIM. CAPERTON WILL CONTINUE TO REPORT TO BARRY SOMMERS, HEAD OF WIM. AS HEAD OF THE PRIVATE BANK, CAPERTON WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR LEADING GROWTH IN THE HIGH NET WORTH AND ULTRA-HIGH NET WO"}{'symbol': 'WFC', 'date': '2021-06-17 13:26:00', 'title': 'OPPORTUNITY FINANCE NETWORK RECEIVES LARGEST GRANT IN 35-YEAR HISTORY FROM WELLS FARGO', 'text': 'WASHINGTON--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- #CDFIS--OPPORTUNITY FINANCE NETWORK (OFN) ANNOUNCED THAT WELLS FARGO IS COMMITTING A $25 MILLION GRANT TO ITS FINANCE JUSTICE FUND TO HELP TACKLE SYSTEMIC BARRIERS TO CAPITAL IN COMMUNITIES AROUND THE COUNTRY. MANAGED BY OPPORTUNITY FINANCE NETWORK, THE FINANCE JUSTICE FUND AIMS TO ADDRESS THE RACIAL WEALTH GAP AND PERSISTENT POVERTY BY DELIVERING FINANCING THROUGH COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS (CDFIS) TO BLACK, LATINX, NATIVE, RURAL, AND OTHER COMMUNITIES WI'}